\subsection*{1. Piecewise response}
The delayed unit step is zero for $t<2$ and one for $t>2$ [1, 2].
The factor $t-2$ vanishes at $t=2$, so the response is zero there
regardless of the convention for $u(0)$. On the requested interval,
\[
f(t)=\begin{cases}
0, & 0\le t<2,\\
(t-2)e^{-(t-2)}, & 2\le t\le 8.
\end{cases}
\]

\subsection*{2. Time and amplitude of the maximum}
Set $x=t-2$ on $2\le t\le8$. Differentiating the active part gives
\[
\frac{d}{dx}(xe^{-x})=e^{-x}-xe^{-x}=(1-x)e^{-x}.
\]
Because $e^{-x}>0$, the response rises for $0<x<1$ and falls for
$1<x\le6$. The global maximum is therefore $f(3)=e^{-1}\approx0.3679$
at $t=3$ [2].

